# The worker image builds from the repository root, because it needs `agents/` alongside the
# API package. Without this file that context is the whole working tree — dependency trees,
# build output, the local virtualenv and the git history — which is slow to send to a local
# daemon and slower still to upload to a remote builder.
#
# Everything here is either reinstalled inside the image, irrelevant to it, or must not be in
# it at all.

# Dependency trees: reinstalled from the lockfiles during the build.
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.venv/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image.
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/out/
dist/
build/

# History and tooling the image has no use for.
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/

# **Never in an image.** `.env` carries the LlamaParse and Azure keys; secrets belong in
# Container Apps secrets, injected at runtime, and an image is copied and cached in a registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# **Patient data.** Dossiers live outside the repository by policy, but a stray copy or a
# rendering check must never be baked into an image that is pushed to a registry.
docs/dossiers/
docs/reference/
**/*.docx
**/~$*

# Local scratch and measurement output.
data/
blobs/
*.log
